PD240W host unit tests (PlatformIO + doctest)
=============================================

Host-side tests for the pure, SDK-free logic headers in src/logic/. They build
for the PC (`platform = native`), not the RP2040, and need no hardware.

Each folder is one suite and one test executable:

  test_cc_regulation/        constant-current regulator math (logic/cc_regulation.h)
  test_pd_diagnostics/       PD diagnostics + EPR exit FSM (logic/pd_diagnostics.h)
  test_programmable_tuning/  PPS/AVS tuning (logic/programmable_tuning.h)
  test_settings_storage/     settings blob, CRC, migrations, fuzz (logic/settings_storage.h)
  test_thermal_monitor/      overtemperature FSM (logic/thermal_monitor.h)

doctest_main.h holds the shared main(); every suite starts with

  #define DOCTEST_CONFIG_IMPLEMENT
  #include <doctest.h>
  #include "doctest_main.h"

Running
-------

  pio test -e native                        all suites
  pio test -e native -f test_thermal_monitor   one suite
  pio test -e native -v                     full doctest output

The native env needs a host g++ on PATH. On Windows with MinGW-w64:

  $env:PATH = "C:\mingw64\bin;$env:PATH"; pio test -e native

Adding a suite
--------------

Create test/test_<name>/test_<name>.cpp with the three lines above, include the
logic header under test, and write TEST_CASE / CHECK / REQUIRE / SUBCASE as
usual. A header is testable when nothing it includes pulls in the Pico SDK or
Arduino; extract hardware-coupled types into a plain-data header first.
